 60ZN c  2025Ow01: {+60}Ga was produced via the projectile fragmentation of a   
 60ZN2c  150-MeV/nucleon {+78}Kr primary beam impinging on a 517-mg/cm{+2} thick
 60ZN3c  {+9}Be target, filtered by the NSCL A1900 separator and the radio      
 60ZN4c  frequency fragment separator, identified by B|r-|DE-ToF, and implanted 
 60ZN5c  into a 1-mm-thick 16|*16 DSSD surrounded by the Summing NaI (SuN)      
 60ZN6c  detector. Ions and positrons were detected using the DSSD and |g rays  
 60ZN7c  were detected using the SuN detector. Measured implant-decay time and  
 60ZN8c  space correlations, |g-ray total absorption spectra (TAS), single sum  
 60ZN9c  of segments spectra (SoS), and multiplicity spectra. Deduced |b-feeding
 60ZNAc  intensity at various excitation energies by fitting simulated TAS, SoS,
 60ZNBc  and multiplicity spectra to data. Deduced T{-1/2} of parent {+60}Ga.   
 60ZNCc  Compared with shell-model calculations using GXPF1A and KB3G           
 60ZNDc  Hamiltonians.                                                          
